## Timeout fix (night re-run prep)

Date: 2026-08-22. Diagnosis correction: night-bench "operation timed out"
trials hit OllamaClient (client.rs, /api/chat), NOT CloudClient. Measured
last-agent-log→trial-finish gaps across the 24 errored polyglot trials
(jobs/2026-08-22__03-07-15): median 335s, dominant cluster 313–337s ⇒ the
effective per-request limit was OllamaClient's fixed **300s**, not 120s.
(120s + "must be 120s" test cited in the diagnosis live in cloud.rs
CloudClient — patched too, same env var.)

### Change
- client.rs: new pub consts `ENV_TIMEOUT_SECS = "KITTY_OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_SECS"`,
  `DEFAULT_OLLAMA_TIMEOUT_SECS = 300`; pure `pub fn parse_timeout_secs(
  raw: Option<&str>, default: u64) -> u64` (missing/empty/unparsable →
  default). OllamaClient::new reads env at construction, stores timeout,
  new accessor `timeout()`. Module docs updated.
- cloud.rs: CloudClient::new same wiring with `DEFAULT_CLOUD_TIMEOUT_SECS =
  120`; accessor returns stored value instead of hardcoded 120s. Docs updated.
  Same env var drives both clients (different defaults).
- Tests target the PURE fn (no process-env mutation → parallel-safe), plus
  kept construction assertions: ollama default 300s, cloud default 120s.

